e list. Every re-wiring gate must count *wired terminals*. This is a live candidate for what killed v3→v7 silently.\n- The queue donor must be a real **node**: a diagram constant, a scalar control terminal and a cluster control terminal are all measured refused, and no built op reads `Terminal.DataType`. The donor question becomes a trial census, and it waits behind S3.\n\n**I got one thing wrong and the retrospective caught it.** I opened by reading cycle 51's build log while it was still being written, concluded the child had been killed, and spent an 825 s re-verification on gates that were passing as I read — bgrun's breakaway detach had kept the child alive and it finished normally at 04:06. Accepted as `inference-over-measurement`, corrected in all three places I had written it, and generalised as Pre-decided 37(j): a log is not evidence until its terminal line is present. I also withdrew my ruling that the P6 failed prediction needed no peer review — that was judgement overriding a mechanical rule, and the review is now a prerequisite to the S3 build.\n\nThe second violation, `device-failed`, I had found independently: `guard_peer`'s `FAILURE_RE` cannot see the `**FAIL**` the new diagnostics print, so the mandatory-review gate has been passing failing runs. Repair queued at both ends.\n\n**NEXT**: P6 review → build S3 (`claudeDev\\D1_s3_loop15.vi`, the whole 1.5 set moved and re-wired, one save) → repair `guard_peer`. Nothing else gates it; lock released, ORIGINAL unchanged, no VI was run.","ttft_ms":3892,"type":"result","duration_ms":6479250,"uuid":"30c9ef53-c0d0-43e9-a6f2-eefdb735549e","ttft_stream_ms":3562,"time_to_request_ms":187,"queued_turn_count":0}
